  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Essential Primary Healthcare Services in the Northwest Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will complement existing projects in the Northwest of Myanmar, to reduce excess mortality and morbidity among vulnerable conflict-affected populations in Chin, Magway and Sagaing by increasing access to, and reducing barriers in accessing, lifesaving health care services through mobile clinics delivering primary health services, with linked outreach activities, including health promotion and education, mental health and psychosocial support (MHPSS) awareness and capacity building, and the provision of medicines and medical supplies. The project will improve access to essential primary healthcare services to both internally displaced persons (IDPs) and host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
